        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chester Erskine, Sam Taylor, William Anthony McGuire\n- Films: A Girl in Every Port, Out All Night\n- Roles: director, writer, producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: Hollywood, Broadway, silent film era\n\nFacts:\n- Sam Taylor was born on August 13, 1895, in New York City and was a film director, screenwriter, and producer most active in the silent film era.\n- Chester Erskine was born on November 29, 1905, and was a Hollywood and Broadway director, writer, and producer.\n- Out All Night is a 1933 American comedy film directed by Sam Taylor and written by William Anthony McGuire.\n- A Girl in Every Port is a 1952 comedy film directed by Chester Erskine.\n- Sam Taylor died on March 6, 1958, in Santa Monica.\n- Chester Erskine died on April 7, 1986.",
